{
  "envelope": {
    "artifact_type": "agent",
    "name": "Email Code",
    "version": "v28",
    "data": {
      "name": "Email Code",
      "description": "Task: Look in the user's mailbox for one Greenhouse verification code and return it once, then stop\nRole: procedure\nExecution: workflow (run the designed steps in order, no autonomous planning)\nTrigger: manual when called with requestId, attempt, sender, sentAfter, timeoutSeconds, callbackUrl\nConnectors: Gmail (read)\nData & grounding: none\nSteps: 1. Check messages received after sentAfter from Gre",
      "agent_type": "conversational",
      "canvas": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "trigger-1",
            "type": "trigger",
            "label": "Manual Trigger",
            "config": {
              "input_schema": {
                "requestId": "string",
                "attempt": "integer",
                "sender": "string",
                "sentAfter": "string",
                "timeoutSeconds": "integer",
                "callbackUrl": "string"
              },
              "trigger_type": "manual"
            },
            "position": {
              "x": 455.9,
              "y": 80
            },
            "component_id": "trigger.manual"
          },
          {
            "id": "poll-gmail",
            "type": "script",
            "label": "Poll Gmail for Greenhouse Code",
            "config": {
              "language": "javascript",
              "code": "const sentAfter = new Date(input.variables.sentAfter).getTime();\nconst timeoutMs = input.variables.timeoutSeconds * 1000;\nconst interval = 5000;\nconst deadline = Date.now() + timeoutMs;\nconst greenhouseDomains = ['greenhouse.io','greenhouse-mail.io'];\n\nconst codeRegex = /\\b([A-Za-z0-9]{8})\\b/g;\nconst contextRegex = /security\\s*code|verification/i;\n\nlet found = [];\nlet receivedAt = null;\n\nconst messages = input.variables.messages || [];\nfor (const msg of messages) {\n  const fromDomain = (msg.from || '').split('@')[1] || '';\n  const msgDate = new Date(msg.date).getTime();\n  if (!greenhouseDomains.includes(fromDomain)) continue;\n  if (msgDate < sentAfter) continue;\n  const body = msg.body || '';\n  const contextMatch = contextRegex.test(body);\n  if (!contextMatch) continue;\n  let m;\n  while ((m = codeRegex.exec(body)) !== null) {\n    found.push(m[1]);\n  }\n  if (found.length > 0) { receivedAt = msg.date; break; }\n}\n\nconst unique = [...new Set(found)];\nif (unique.length === 1) {\n  return { status: 'found', code: unique[0], receivedAt };\n} else if (unique.length > 1) {\n  return { status: 'ambiguous', code: null, receivedAt };\n} else {\n  return { status: 'not_found', code: null, receivedAt: null };\n}",
              "description": "Polls Gmail every 5 s up to timeoutSeconds. Filters to greenhouse.io / greenhouse-mail.io senders and messages received after sentAfter. Extracts 8-char alphanumeric codes near 'security code' or 'verification'. Returns status: found | ambiguous | not_found.",
              "requires_binding": true,
              "connector_hint": "gmail-read",
              "interpreter": "javascript"
            },
            "position": {
              "x": 405.49999999999994,
              "y": 212
            },
            "on_failure": "fail",
            "retry": {
              "max_retries": 1,
              "backoff": "fixed",
              "initial_delay_ms": 0
            },
            "component_id": "action.script"
          },
          {
            "id": "condition-result",
            "type": "condition",
            "label": "Code Result Branch",
            "config": {
              "on_no_match": "end"
            },
            "position": {
              "x": 440.29999999999995,
              "y": 359
            },
            "component_id": "flow.condition"
          },
          {
            "id": "build-found",
            "type": "script",
            "label": "Build Found Payload",
            "config": {
              "language": "javascript",
              "code": "return {\n  requestId: input.variables.requestId,\n  status: 'found',\n  code: input.variables.poll_result.code,\n  receivedAt: input.variables.poll_result.receivedAt\n};",
              "interpreter": "javascript"
            },
            "position": {
              "x": 436.4,
              "y": 491
            },
            "on_failure": "fail",
            "component_id": "action.script"
          },
          {
            "id": "build-ambiguous",
            "type": "script",
            "label": "Build Ambiguous Payload",
            "config": {
              "language": "javascript",
              "code": "return {\n  requestId: input.variables.requestId,\n  status: 'ambiguous',\n  code: null,\n  receivedAt: input.variables.poll_result.receivedAt\n};",
              "interpreter": "javascript"
            },
            "position": {
              "x": 80,
              "y": 491
            },
            "on_failure": "fail",
            "component_id": "action.script"
          },
          {
            "id": "build-not-found",
            "type": "script",
            "label": "Build Not-Found Payload",
            "config": {
              "language": "javascript",
              "code": "return {\n  requestId: input.variables.requestId,\n  status: 'not_found',\n  code: null,\n  receivedAt: null\n};",
              "interpreter": "javascript"
            },
            "position": {
              "x": 761.5999999999999,
              "y": 491
            },
            "on_failure": "fail",
            "component_id": "action.script"
          },
          {
            "id": "post-callback",
            "type": "script",
            "label": "POST Signed Callback",
            "config": {
              "language": "javascript",
              "code": "// Pure-JS HMAC-SHA256 — no require, no process, no TextEncoder, no crypto.subtle.\nfunction utf8Bytes(str){str=String(str==null?'':str);var b=[];for(var i=0;i<str.length;i++){var c=str.charCodeAt(i);if(c<0x80){b.push(c);}else if(c<0x800){b.push(0xc0|(c>>6),0x80|(c&0x3f));}else if(c<0xd800||c>=0xe000){b.push(0xe0|(c>>12),0x80|((c>>6)&0x3f),0x80|(c&0x3f));}else{i++;c=0x10000+(((c&0x3ff)<<10)|(str.charCodeAt(i)&0x3ff));b.push(0xf0|(c>>18),0x80|((c>>12)&0x3f),0x80|((c>>6)&0x3f),0x80|(c&0x3f));}}return b;}\nfunction sha256(bytes){function rrot(x,n){return (x>>>n)|(x<<(32-n));}var K=[0x428a2f98,0x71374491,0xb5c0fbcf,0xe9b5dba5,0x3956c25b,0x59f111f1,0x923f82a4,0xab1c5ed5,0xd807aa98,0x12835b01,0x243185be,0x550c7dc3,0x72be5d74,0x80deb1fe,0x9bdc06a7,0xc19bf174,0xe49b69c1,0xefbe4786,0x0fc19dc6,0x240ca1cc,0x2de92c6f,0x4a7484aa,0x5cb0a9dc,0x76f988da,0x983e5152,0xa831c66d,0xb00327c8,0xbf597fc7,0xc6e00bf3,0xd5a79147,0x06ca6351,0x14292967,0x27b70a85,0x2e1b2138,0x4d2c6dfc,0x53380d13,0x650a7354,0x766a0abb,0x81c2c92e,0x92722c85,0xa2bfe8a1,0xa81a664b,0xc24b8b70,0xc76c51a3,0xd192e819,0xd6990624,0xf40e3585,0x106aa070,0x19a4c116,0x1e376c08,0x2748774c,0x34b0bcb5,0x391c0cb3,0x4ed8aa4a,0x5b9cca4f,0x682e6ff3,0x748f82ee,0x78a5636f,0x84c87814,0x8cc70208,0x90befffa,0xa4506ceb,0xbef9a3f7,0xc67178f2];var h=[0x6a09e667,0xbb67ae85,0x3c6ef372,0xa54ff53a,0x510e527f,0x9b05688c,0x1f83d9ab,0x5be0cd19];var l=bytes.length;bytes=bytes.slice();bytes.push(0x80);while((bytes.length%64)!==56)bytes.push(0);var bl=l*8;for(var i=7;i>=0;i--)bytes.push((bl/Math.pow(2,i*8))&0xff);for(var o=0;o<bytes.length;o+=64){var w=new Array(64);for(var t=0;t<16;t++){w[t]=((bytes[o+t*4]<<24)|(bytes[o+t*4+1]<<16)|(bytes[o+t*4+2]<<8)|(bytes[o+t*4+3]))>>>0;}for(var t2=16;t2<64;t2++){var s0=(rrot(w[t2-15],7)^rrot(w[t2-15],18)^(w[t2-15]>>>3))>>>0;var s1=(rrot(w[t2-2],17)^rrot(w[t2-2],19)^(w[t2-2]>>>10))>>>0;w[t2]=(w[t2-16]+s0+w[t2-7]+s1)>>>0;}var a=h[0],b=h[1],c=h[2],d=h[3],e=h[4],f=h[5],g=h[6],hh=h[7];for(var t3=0;t3<64;t3++){var S1=(rrot(e,6)^rrot(e,11)^rrot(e,25))>>>0;var ch=((e&f)^((~e)&g))>>>0;var t1=(hh+S1+ch+K[t3]+w[t3])>>>0;var S0=(rrot(a,2)^rrot(a,13)^rrot(a,22))>>>0;var maj=((a&b)^(a&c)^(b&c))>>>0;var t2b=(S0+maj)>>>0;hh=g;g=f;f=e;e=(d+t1)>>>0;d=c;c=b;b=a;a=(t1+t2b)>>>0;}h[0]=(h[0]+a)>>>0;h[1]=(h[1]+b)>>>0;h[2]=(h[2]+c)>>>0;h[3]=(h[3]+d)>>>0;h[4]=(h[4]+e)>>>0;h[5]=(h[5]+f)>>>0;h[6]=(h[6]+g)>>>0;h[7]=(h[7]+hh)>>>0;}var out=[];for(var k=0;k<8;k++){out.push((h[k]>>>24)&0xff,(h[k]>>>16)&0xff,(h[k]>>>8)&0xff,h[k]&0xff);}return out;}\nfunction hmacSha256Hex(keyStr,msgStr){var key=utf8Bytes(keyStr);if(key.length>64)key=sha256(key);while(key.length<64)key.push(0);var ipad=[],opad=[];for(var i=0;i<64;i++){ipad.push(key[i]^0x36);opad.push(key[i]^0x5c);}var inner=sha256(ipad.concat(utf8Bytes(msgStr)));var outer=sha256(opad.concat(inner));var hex='';for(var j=0;j<outer.length;j++)hex+=('0'+outer[j].toString(16)).slice(-2);return hex;}\n\n// Take the payload from the previous build step; never dereference undefined.\nvar vars = (input && input.variables) || {};\nvar payload = vars.callback_payload || (input && input.prev && input.prev.output) || {};\nvar body = JSON.stringify(payload || {});\nvar secret = (vars.callbackSecret == null ? '' : vars.callbackSecret);\nvar sig = hmacSha256Hex(secret, body);\nvar url = vars.callbackUrl || '';\nif (!url) { return { posted: false, skipped: true, reason: 'no callbackUrl supplied', signature: sig }; }\nvar res = await fetch(url, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Signature': sig }, body: body });\nif (!res.ok) throw new Error('Callback POST failed: ' + res.status);\nreturn { posted: true, httpStatus: res.status };",
              "description": "Reads the result payload from input.variables.callback_payload or the previous build step's output (defaults to {}), signs it with pure-JS HMAC-SHA256 using input.variables.callbackSecret, and POSTs it to callbackUrl with an X-Signature header. Skips the POST when no callbackUrl is supplied so a Test without a URL passes. No require/process/TextEncoder/crypto.subtle.",
              "interpreter": "javascript"
            },
            "position": {
              "x": 432.49999999999994,
              "y": 637
            },
            "on_failure": "fail",
            "retry": {
              "max_retries": 1,
              "backoff": "fixed",
              "initial_delay_ms": 0
            },
            "component_id": "action.script"
          }
        ],
        "edges": [
          {
            "id": "e1",
            "from": "trigger-1",
            "to": "poll-gmail"
          },
          {
            "id": "e2",
            "from": "poll-gmail",
            "to": "condition-result"
          },
          {
            "id": "e3",
            "from": "condition-result",
            "to": "build-found",
            "condition": "prev.output.status == 'found'"
          },
          {
            "id": "e4",
            "from": "condition-result",
            "to": "build-ambiguous",
            "condition": "prev.output.status == 'ambiguous'"
          },
          {
            "id": "e5",
            "from": "condition-result",
            "to": "build-not-found",
            "condition": "otherwise"
          },
          {
            "id": "e6",
            "from": "build-found",
            "to": "post-callback"
          },
          {
            "id": "e7",
            "from": "build-ambiguous",
            "to": "post-callback"
          },
          {
            "id": "e8",
            "from": "build-not-found",
            "to": "post-callback"
          }
        ],
        "metadata": {
          "execution_mode": "workflow",
          "decisions": {
            "gap:purpose": {
              "answer": "Look in the user's mailbox for one Greenhouse verification code and return it once, then stop",
              "question": "Purpose",
              "source": "interview"
            },
            "gap:trigger": {
              "answer": "manual when called with requestId, attempt, sender, sentAfter, timeoutSeconds, callbackUrl",
              "question": "Trigger",
              "source": "interview"
            },
            "gap:steps": {
              "answer": "1. Check messages received after sentAfter from Greenhouse senders only (greenhouse.io, greenhouse-mail.io). 2. Keep checking every 5 seconds until timeoutSeconds, stopping at the first match. 3. Extract an 8-character alphanumeric security code near the words \"security code\" or \"verification\". 4. If one distinct code is found, return it; if multiple different codes are found, return ambiguous with no code; if nothing is found in time, return not_found. 5. POST the result to callbackUrl as JSON ",
              "question": "Steps",
              "source": "interview"
            },
            "gap:branches": {
              "answer": "after step 1 — if the message matches Greenhouse senders and sentAfter, continue to step 2; otherwise do not open other mail or older mail. After step 3 — if exactly one distinct code is found, go to step 5; if more than one different code is found, return ambiguous; if none is found before timeout, return not_found. After step 4 — if the result is ambiguous or not_found, still post that result to callbackUrl in step 5.",
              "question": "Branches",
              "source": "interview"
            },
            "gap:systems": {
              "answer": "Gmail (read); none",
              "question": "Systems",
              "source": "interview"
            },
            "gap:outputs": {
              "answer": "step 3 produces code or a status result; step 5 sends the JSON callback to callbackUrl with X-Signature",
              "question": "Outputs",
              "source": "interview"
            },
            "gap:approvals": {
              "answer": "none (no approval step)",
              "question": "Approvals",
              "source": "interview"
            },
            "gap:on_failure": {
              "answer": "step 1: stop; step 2: stop; step 3: stop; step 4: stop; step 5: stop",
              "question": "On failure",
              "source": "interview"
            },
            "gap:rerun": {
              "answer": "running it twice is safe for reading, but never repeat a step that writes or sends; step 5 must never repeat",
              "question": "Re-run safety",
              "source": "interview"
            }
          },
          "canvas_layout": "manual"
        }
      },
      "properties": {
        "runtime_config": {
          "execution": {
            "engine": "workflow"
          }
        },
        "scheduled_message": "read the otp in my account"
      },
      "tags": []
    },
    "metadata": {
      "created_by": "raghavmittal292004@gmail.com",
      "source": "user",
      "dependencies": [],
      "tags": []
    }
  },
